  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "All transferable gold-domain records visible at L1/L2 report oral bioavailability values at or above the F=20% threshold (thalidomide 80–100%, eltoprazine ~95% and 102±29%/110±32%, imipramine-N-oxide 100%, bexagliflozin ~78%, pethidine in cirrhosis 0.80, SB-742457 excellent/76% in rat and 24% in rat, CAB near-complete); no affirmative sub-20% value is present.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10","C11","C12","C13","C14","C15","C18","C19","C21","C23","C26","C27"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records show measurable systemic exposure in humans for related piperazine antipsychotics (trazodone AUC ~10.07–10.44 µg·h/mL and Cmax ~1.61–1.66 µg/mL; cariprazine 1.5 mg Cmax 882 pg/mL; ziprasidone fed AUCinf ~1045 ng·h/mL), supporting oral absorption but not directly quantifying F.",
      "card_ids": ["C28","C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C36","C37","C38","C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 absorption/permeability records for related scaffolds are supportive: the cilostazol-like M02 with the same dihydroquinolinone butoxy linker is >95% absorbed in rats and highly permeable by Caco-2/animal/human studies, and cetirizine shows high human intestinal absorption; DMP shows high solubility in Tween 20 and complete SEDDS dissolution.",
      "card_ids": ["C42","C43","C45","C46","C47","C49"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall/intestinal-metabolism records are mostly permeability-supportive (buspirone Papp 398 nm/s highest among CYP3A4 substrates; DMP Papp >1×10^-5 cm/s; MF-8rac 25.6×10^-6 cm/s; tandospirone good permeability; imipramine ~10^-5 cm/s) and include only modest mechanistic efflux/metabolism signals (compound 29 efflux ratio 1.8; MF-8B Pgp stimulation; GL-V9 extensive liver metabolism) that do not affirm F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C53","C54","C55","C56","C57","C58","C59","C60","C61","C62","C63"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement is present; the decision relies on transfer from related high-F contexts.",
    "No query-specific measured solubility or permeability is supplied; the query's high logD (4.39) and neutral fraction 0.34 leave a dissolution risk.",
    "No query-specific first-pass metabolism or clearance data are supplied; the high prediction assumes no disproportionate first-pass effect.",
    "L5 efflux/metabolism records are from related molecules (buspirone, MF-8, GL-V9, compound 29), not the query, and are mechanistic only.",
    "C29's low-exposure signal lacks an IV comparator, dose-linearity, and assay-sensitivity context, so it cannot be interpreted as F<20%.",
    "SB-742457 has conflicting rat bioavailability values (24% vs 76%), adding species/formulation uncertainty."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: all transferable gold-domain F records are >=20% (mostly 76–110%), L3 shows measurable oral exposure for related piperazine antipsychotics, L4 adds supportive absorption/permeability evidence, and L5 adds mostly high-permeability data with only modest mechanistic efflux/metabolism signals that do not affirm F<20%. Confidence remains moderate because no direct query-specific F, solubility, or first-pass measurement is available."
}

